# sign-extension — environment template
#
# Copy this file to .env (or to .env.coston / .env.coston2 and switch with
# `./scripts/use-chain.sh <chain>`). The active .env is loaded by every script.
#
# The essential variables for a Coston/Coston2 deploy are grouped at the top.
# Each one is explained under "Essential variables explained" below; optional /
# advanced variables come after that.

# === Essential variables ====================================================
CHAIN=coston2
CHAIN_URL=https://coston2-api.flare.network/ext/C/rpc
ADDRESSES_FILE=./config/coston2/deployed-addresses.json
NORMAL_PROXY_URL=https://tee-proxy-coston2-1.flare.rocks
EXT_PROXY_URL=

LOCAL_MODE=false
SIMULATED_TEE=false
DEPLOYMENT_PRIVATE_KEY="<your-funded-private-key-hex-no-0x>"
INITIAL_OWNER="0x<your-address>"

# TEE governance — the signer set + threshold that governs this extension's TEE
# machines. post-build registers it on-chain (set-governance) AND the TEE node
# signs with it; both read these same vars, so they always agree. If unset,
# defaults to GOVERNANCE_SIGNERS=<INITIAL_OWNER> (the deployer) and
# GOVERNANCE_THRESHOLD=1. Set your own to use a different governance set:
# GOVERNANCE_SIGNERS="0xAbc...,0xDef..."   # comma-separated 0x addresses
# GOVERNANCE_THRESHOLD=2

LANGUAGE=go

# === Essential variables explained ==========================================
#
# CHAIN
#   coston | coston2 | local. Also used by scripts to pick the addresses file.
#
# CHAIN_URL
#   Chain RPC URL.
#     Coston:       https://coston-api.flare.network/ext/C/rpc
#     Coston2:      https://coston2-api.flare.network/ext/C/rpc
#     Local devnet: http://127.0.0.1:8545
#
# ADDRESSES_FILE
#   Path to the on-chain contract registry for this chain (array+Diamond format).
#
# NORMAL_PROXY_URL
#   Normal/FTDC proxy URL on the target chain. Used during register-tee for the
#   availability check.
#     Coston:  https://tee-proxy-coston-1.flare.rocks
#     Coston2: https://tee-proxy-coston2-1.flare.rocks
#
# EXT_PROXY_URL
#   Extension proxy URL — the host that exposes /info and /action. Leave empty
#   for a Coston/Coston2 deploy until devops hands the URL back after the VM
#   deploy. For local Docker compose this auto-detects to http://localhost:6674.
#
# LOCAL_MODE
#   true for local devnet, false for Coston/Coston2.
#
# SIMULATED_TEE
#   Attestation mode. true on local devnet (test code hash), false on a real GCP
#   Confidential Space VM. Must agree with the TEE binary's MODE env
#   (1=simulated, 0=production attestation).
#
# DEPLOYMENT_PRIVATE_KEY
#   Funded private key used by deploy + register tools (no 0x prefix). Must hold
#   C2FLR/CFLR on the target chain — fund at https://faucet.flare.network/
#
# INITIAL_OWNER
#   Address derived from DEPLOYMENT_PRIVATE_KEY — becomes the extension owner.
#
# LANGUAGE
#   Extension language: go | python | typescript. Picks which Dockerfile
#   docker-compose builds for the extension-tee service. The Go path is the most
#   thoroughly reproducible; python/typescript aim for same-machine determinism
#   (see REPRODUCIBILITY.md).

# === Optional / advanced ====================================================

# Private key the local ext-proxy signs relayed instructions with.
#
# Left empty on purpose. `scripts/new-testnet-keys.sh` generates a fresh
# disposable one into .env, which is gitignored. The upstream fce-sign example
# shipped a real, heavily-used shared testnet key here; committing a working key
# to an example file is how they end up pasted into places that do hold value, so
# it is not reproduced.
PROXY_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# Docker image registry. Leave commented to use the locally-built local/tee-proxy
# image (see scripts/start-services.sh). Set to a remote registry to pull instead.
# REGISTRY=registry.gitlab.com/flarenetwork/tee/e2e
